(1911803, 263986, 46586, '<td valign="top">Hmmm...I don''t know what note to put on this picture...There''s no point in focus but it doesn''t block the lecture of the picture: everybody understand what it is...<br/>and I like the colors too...It''s really not easy. I would say a 6...</td>', 'Hmmm...I don''t know what note to put on this picture...There''s no point in focus but it doesn''t block the lecture of the picture: everybody understand what it is...and I like the colors too...It''s really not easy. I would say a 6...', '2005-12-01 09:40:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1911807, 257093, 42456, '<td valign="top">rotate background to horizontal...as I was told by one of my instructors, " A portrait is like a ansel adams landscape and the eyes it''s most important feature."</td>', 'rotate background to horizontal...as I was told by one of my instructors, " A portrait is like a ansel adams landscape and the eyes it''s most important feature."', '2005-12-01 09:41:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1911808, 264068, 43463, '<td valign="top">An interesting shot and composition. I like how you took this from an angle that has the viewer looking up to gaze on the main subject: the windmill. There are two things that I can suggest that would go into improving this shot. First, it would have been better to capture the full windmill so that it adds to our sense of height as we look up at it. Second, there is too much empty space which does nothing to add to the composition of the overall image - the clouds are nothing special in this shot, your main focus is the windmill and should stay on the windmill. Tightly cropping the shot to be a vertical one that has the windmill either in the center or slightly off center would add interest by giving us a greater sense of height, keeping our attention focused on the main subject, and the vertical aspect mimics &amp; complements the height of the windmill.</td>', 'An interesting shot and composition. I like how you took this from an angle that has the viewer looking up to gaze on the main subject: the windmill. There are two things that I can suggest that would go into improving this shot. First, it would have been better to capture the full windmill so that it adds to our sense of height as we look up at it. Second, there is too much empty space which does nothing to add to the composition of the overall image - the clouds are nothing special in this shot, your main focus is the windmill and should stay on the windmill. Tightly cropping the shot to be a vertical one that has the windmill either in the center or slightly off center would add interest by giving us a greater sense of height, keeping our attention focused on the main subject, and the vertical aspect mimics & complements the height of the windmill.', '2005-12-01 09:41:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1911809, 262911, 39158, '<td valign="top">great colors</td>', 'great colors', '2005-12-01 09:41:23.000000', NULL, 1),
