(1912905, 263227, 39038, '<td valign="top">I would try it again with a smaller aperture value, say F22? if that still can not get everything in focus, I will pull camera back further. I really wanted to see everything in focus, clear and sharp.<br/> <br/>I have been too picky though. This is one of the few excellent photos I have seen so far!<br/> <br/>Great work!</td>', 'I would try it again with a smaller aperture value, say F22? if that still can not get everything in focus, I will pull camera back further. I really wanted to see everything in focus, clear and sharp. I have been too picky though. This is one of the few excellent photos I have seen so far! Great work!', '2005-12-01 14:10:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1912906, 263277, 45115, '<td valign="top">I can see you have worked really hard in finding a striking subject for that free study! Well done!</td>', 'I can see you have worked really hard in finding a striking subject for that free study! Well done!', '2005-12-01 14:10:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1912907, 259342, 2612, '<td valign="top">When I first saw this in thumbnail size I was expecting an almost cliche glamour shot. I was pleasantly surprised to find that your interpretation had much more depth. The pose is provides a nice shape without be exagerated. The subjects head being down adds a sense of mystery... not who is she, but what or who is she thinking about. The detail in the hands and highlights on the hair are nice touches.<br/> <br/>My only artistic question would be why lower part of her left leg completely lost in the shadow? Just enough separation between leg and wall to provide a shape/line through the bottom of the frame would have helped to balance against her right leg. Very minor really, but it''s the only thing question I had.</td>', 'When I first saw this in thumbnail size I was expecting an almost cliche glamour shot. I was pleasantly surprised to find that your interpretation had much more depth. The pose is provides a nice shape without be exagerated. The subjects head being down adds a sense of mystery... not who is she, but what or who is she thinking about. The detail in the hands and highlights on the hair are nice touches. My only artistic question would be why lower part of her left leg completely lost in the shadow? Just enough separation between leg and wall to provide a shape/line through the bottom of the frame would have helped to balance against her right leg. Very minor really, but it''s the only thing question I had.', '2005-12-01 14:10:58.000000', NULL, 1),
