(1934542, 263048, 41845, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. Just perfect in its isolation.  Congrats JP great entry!</td>', 'Beautiful. Just perfect in its isolation.  Congrats JP great entry!', '2005-12-08 09:09:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934547, 261658, 15711, '<td valign="top">Top 10 WOO HOO - that''s quite a feather in your cap, considering the competition!!!</td>', 'Top 10 WOO HOO - that''s quite a feather in your cap, considering the competition!!!', '2005-12-08 09:11:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934548, 263137, 6900, '<td valign="top">Not Rikki, but thanks. :)  <br/> <br/>This was for a client - she bought this pose (and 12 or so more) out of 49 so I''m happy with the image.  :)  It''s got exactly what I wanted going on - poppin eyes, a little bit of hair shaping her face and almost enough body to see what''s going on.  It also has almost no post processing except the eyes.  The rest of the photo looks exactly how I took it.<br/> <br/>Oh, for all the comments and voters who thought "it''s blown out" please download the image on your screen, open it in photoshop and use curves to darken the image on your screen.  There are VERY FEW areas that are blown out - a touch on her forehead, a touch on the background.  There''s detail there and if you can''t see it, calibrate.  Photoshop can see it.  I can see it.  <br/> <br/>Enjoy!</td>', 'Not Rikki, but thanks. :)   This was for a client - she bought this pose (and 12 or so more) out of 49 so I''m happy with the image.  :)  It''s got exactly what I wanted going on - poppin eyes, a little bit of hair shaping her face and almost enough body to see what''s going on.  It also has almost no post processing except the eyes.  The rest of the photo looks exactly how I took it. Oh, for all the comments and voters who thought "it''s blown out" please download the image on your screen, open it in photoshop and use curves to darken the image on your screen.  There are VERY FEW areas that are blown out - a touch on her forehead, a touch on the background.  There''s detail there and if you can''t see it, calibrate.  Photoshop can see it.  I can see it.   Enjoy!', '2005-12-08 09:11:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934549, 260082, 15711, '<td valign="top">Congrats again, dude.  Nice work</td>', 'Congrats again, dude.  Nice work', '2005-12-08 09:12:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934550, 261658, 41845, '<td valign="top">Top 10 in an amazing challenge - well deserved.  This is just captivating. Congrats Doc.</td>', 'Top 10 in an amazing challenge - well deserved.  This is just captivating. Congrats Doc.', '2005-12-08 09:12:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934552, 262310, 15711, '<td valign="top">I''m a black background fan too!!  Congrats on your high placement.  What a wonderful model! Give grandpa a hug from me.</td>', 'I''m a black background fan too!!  Congrats on your high placement.  What a wonderful model! Give grandpa a hug from me.', '2005-12-08 09:13:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934554, 260205, 4226, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Falc:</b></div><hr/><i> I was sure this was oil - very neat </i></td></tr></table> <br/>hmm oil ? I used water. My first thoughts were to use oil, but density of oil is less than water, also I am not sure how the surface tension of oil is, will it support or not ?</td>', 'Originally posted by Falc: I was sure this was oil - very neat  hmm oil ? I used water. My first thoughts were to use oil, but density of oil is less than water, also I am not sure how the surface tension of oil is, will it support or not ?', '2005-12-08 09:14:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1934555, 263940, 15711, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your high finish. I think it deserved top 5~~</td>', 'Congrats on your high finish. I think it deserved top 5~~', '2005-12-08 09:14:05.000000', NULL, 0),
