(1936412, 261484, 14620, '<td valign="top">Hey Jason, yes I do like this one.  I gave it a 6 and here''s why (mainly technical stuff), I like photos with shallow DOF, but for some reason the background on this seems just a bit too blurred.  I like his look, it''s very inviting (even with the makeup) :-)  I might off-center him just a bit more if you''re going to go with a horizontal format and I agree with MrsFuzzButt about cropping it so more of his hair was visible, as I think that''s kind of important part of his look.  Also, if this was my shot, I might sharpen his pupils a bit because as it is, his eyebrows &amp; beard seem more in focus and it kind of distracts just a little.  But that''s just a personal preference for me, I really dig super sharp eyes. Overall, I think it''s a nice portrait, you brought out his personality well and it should have scored higher than it did. But Free studies are always tough competitions. :-)</td>', 'Hey Jason, yes I do like this one.  I gave it a 6 and here''s why (mainly technical stuff), I like photos with shallow DOF, but for some reason the background on this seems just a bit too blurred.  I like his look, it''s very inviting (even with the makeup) :-)  I might off-center him just a bit more if you''re going to go with a horizontal format and I agree with MrsFuzzButt about cropping it so more of his hair was visible, as I think that''s kind of important part of his look.  Also, if this was my shot, I might sharpen his pupils a bit because as it is, his eyebrows & beard seem more in focus and it kind of distracts just a little.  But that''s just a personal preference for me, I really dig super sharp eyes. Overall, I think it''s a nice portrait, you brought out his personality well and it should have scored higher than it did. But Free studies are always tough competitions. :-)', '2005-12-08 20:25:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1936474, 256160, 27164, '<td valign="top">Beautiful as always Robert.  I find this photo very interesting in that the flare from the sun is replicated almost exactly in the reflection.  I can''t say that I''ve ever seen this (or noticed it) before in a photo.  Great use of color.  Nice work.</td>', 'Beautiful as always Robert.  I find this photo very interesting in that the flare from the sun is replicated almost exactly in the reflection.  I can''t say that I''ve ever seen this (or noticed it) before in a photo.  Great use of color.  Nice work.', '2005-12-08 20:51:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1936477, 260489, 45579, '<td valign="top">i saw a lot of pictures ranked above yours that weren''t as good as this one.  definitely one of the best from the challenge.</td>', 'i saw a lot of pictures ranked above yours that weren''t as good as this one.  definitely one of the best from the challenge.', '2005-12-08 20:52:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1936479, 263646, 19708, '<td valign="top">Lessons learned:<br/>1) Sports shots don''t do well here. (Thanks Alan - you spoiled it for me) LOL<br/>2) Once in a lifetime shots don''t do well here.<br/>3) A goof shot of steel ball bearings post-processed to hell &amp; back scores<br/>better than a decisive moment of a well-known and gifted athlete.<br/>4) I should go back to shooting flowers or learn grunge PP.<br/> <br/>Oh well, Quentin Jammer''s foundation is interested to see this shot.<br/>THAT is worth more than a good score.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-12-08 21:52:03.</i></td>', 'Lessons learned:1) Sports shots don''t do well here. (Thanks Alan - you spoiled it for me) LOL2) Once in a lifetime shots don''t do well here.3) A goof shot of steel ball bearings post-processed to hell & back scoresbetter than a decisive moment of a well-known and gifted athlete.4) I should go back to shooting flowers or learn grunge PP. Oh well, Quentin Jammer''s foundation is interested to see this shot.THAT is worth more than a good score.', '2005-12-08 20:53:06.000000', '2005-12-08 21:52:03.000000', 0),
