(1939683, 263646, 39243, '<td valign="top">Brad I for one gave you a 9 - probably should have given you a 10.  The clarity and moment of capture are amazing. I know how hard a decent action shot can be, but I have one very very small wish. If Quentin Jammers'' eyes were more exposed that would have been even more amazing. I however do not fault you one tiny tiny bit for not fullfilling my wish. Great Shot. <br/>Steve<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by BradP:</b></div><hr/><i> Lessons learned:<br/>1) Sports shots don''t do well here. (Thanks Alan - you spoiled it for me) LOL<br/>2) Once in a lifetime shots don''t do well here.<br/>3) A goof shot of steel ball bearings post-processed to hell &amp; back scores<br/>better than a decisive moment of a well-known and gifted athlete.<br/>4) I should go back to shooting flowers or learn grunge PP.<br/> <br/>Oh well, Quentin Jammer''s foundation is interested to see this shot.<br/>THAT is worth more than a good score. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Brad I for one gave you a 9 - probably should have given you a 10.  The clarity and moment of capture are amazing. I know how hard a decent action shot can be, but I have one very very small wish. If Quentin Jammers'' eyes were more exposed that would have been even more amazing. I however do not fault you one tiny tiny bit for not fullfilling my wish. Great Shot. Steve Originally posted by BradP: Lessons learned:1) Sports shots don''t do well here. (Thanks Alan - you spoiled it for me) LOL2) Once in a lifetime shots don''t do well here.3) A goof shot of steel ball bearings post-processed to hell & back scoresbetter than a decisive moment of a well-known and gifted athlete.4) I should go back to shooting flowers or learn grunge PP. Oh well, Quentin Jammer''s foundation is interested to see this shot.THAT is worth more than a good score. ', '2005-12-10 01:57:22.000000', NULL, 0),
