(1952299, 264054, 42456, '<td valign="top">''Baking'' was the portrait shot I entered for the Free Study...I picked up some ideas from you on this one. I like your perspective a lot better! I know you put some work into this one...Great Job! Thanks for your feedback on "Just Feedback"</td>', '''Baking'' was the portrait shot I entered for the Free Study...I picked up some ideas from you on this one. I like your perspective a lot better! I know you put some work into this one...Great Job! Thanks for your feedback on "Just Feedback"', '2005-12-14 19:55:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952364, 263437, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I thought this was great when I saw it during the challenge. I remember scoring it very high. Your DOF is spot on IMO. The colors are wonderful. Technically, I think that it is perfect. I have no idea why it didn''t score higher? I guess because there where so many awesome photos in this challenge! It was a real hard one. I love the facial expression. You couldn''t have clicked the shutter at a more perfect time. Way to go! Sorry, that I did not have any suggestions for you. When I see photos like yours I wonder if I should really be a part of the "critique club". <br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I thought this was great when I saw it during the challenge. I remember scoring it very high. Your DOF is spot on IMO. The colors are wonderful. Technically, I think that it is perfect. I have no idea why it didn''t score higher? I guess because there where so many awesome photos in this challenge! It was a real hard one. I love the facial expression. You couldn''t have clicked the shutter at a more perfect time. Way to go! Sorry, that I did not have any suggestions for you. When I see photos like yours I wonder if I should really be a part of the "critique club".  Mandy', '2005-12-14 20:25:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952379, 262911, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Well done! Yet another photo that I have no suggestions for? Why do I always get the perfect pictures to critique? You did really well on the composition. I like the way how you can see the leaves and stem in the background and that is it. The colors POP out at you, but are not too bright or over saturated. Focus, again....awesome. One thing that I really look for in floral pictures are damaged petals.....you have not ONE! This couldn''t have been photographed better! Congrats!<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* Well done! Yet another photo that I have no suggestions for? Why do I always get the perfect pictures to critique? You did really well on the composition. I like the way how you can see the leaves and stem in the background and that is it. The colors POP out at you, but are not too bright or over saturated. Focus, again....awesome. One thing that I really look for in floral pictures are damaged petals.....you have not ONE! This couldn''t have been photographed better! Congrats! Mandy', '2005-12-14 20:29:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952396, 263833, 45793, '<td valign="top">My dream is to be able to take photographs like this one some day..!<br/>BEAUTIFUL!!</td>', 'My dream is to be able to take photographs like this one some day..!BEAUTIFUL!!', '2005-12-14 20:38:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952404, 261412, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Very very interesting! What an amazing site! I would have loved to have seen this in person. I have never been out of the United States, much less Africa. I am so jealous. <br/> <br/>I think that you have captured this scene very well. The purple tones of the sky are magical. The mountain is very interesting as well. It has great texture and seems to change color either from the skies reflection or manipulated by you...doesn''t matter...its cool! The subject for the challenge was a good one! I also feel that this image has alot of appeal to it. <br/> <br/>The one thing that I might have done differently would have been the crop. Now, I am not an expert or claim to be. I do not photograph landscapes either. This is just my opinion. I would have zoomed in closer to the mountain and let IT take up about 1/2  or 3/4 of the frame. Cropping it just a little bit above the highest peak of the mountain. The reason is because, I personally find the colors and texture of the mountain more appealing than the sky. The sky is beautiful, but for me, the clouds do not seem to hold enough of my interest to take up more than half of the frame. <br/> <br/>I hope that this was helpful. Please forgive my spelling..I am just a hick from Tennessee. LOL<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* Very very interesting! What an amazing site! I would have loved to have seen this in person. I have never been out of the United States, much less Africa. I am so jealous.  I think that you have captured this scene very well. The purple tones of the sky are magical. The mountain is very interesting as well. It has great texture and seems to change color either from the skies reflection or manipulated by you...doesn''t matter...its cool! The subject for the challenge was a good one! I also feel that this image has alot of appeal to it.  The one thing that I might have done differently would have been the crop. Now, I am not an expert or claim to be. I do not photograph landscapes either. This is just my opinion. I would have zoomed in closer to the mountain and let IT take up about 1/2  or 3/4 of the frame. Cropping it just a little bit above the highest peak of the mountain. The reason is because, I personally find the colors and texture of the mountain more appealing than the sky. The sky is beautiful, but for me, the clouds do not seem to hold enough of my interest to take up more than half of the frame.  I hope that this was helpful. Please forgive my spelling..I am just a hick from Tennessee. LOL Mandy', '2005-12-14 20:42:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952437, 264088, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I LOVE the colors! Very Nice!! I think that the lighting (contrast) is perfect too. Wouldn''t change it at ALL. <br/> <br/>There are a few things I would change. Is that a light pole? There is a really tall pole or something behind or infront of the tree on the right. I would have cloned that out. I also would have cloned out the bridge in the background. It is a nice bridge...but doesn''t say wild safari to me. <br/> <br/>The trees and the coloration of the sky combined with the sunset scream safari to me though. Reminds me of the beginning of The Lion King movie. Can you tell that I have small children?<br/> <br/>As far as the compostion goes, I think that you did a fine job. I held up a piece of paper and "cropped" off some on the left side where the negative space is. My thoughts were..."nope, looks better like it is!" With the negative space gone the picture looks too centered and boring. <br/> <br/>The sun looks a little strange. I guess because I expect it to be a circle. Not sure how the two bumps on it happened....it was just something I noticed.<br/> <br/>Overall...I like the photograph! It is very pleasing to look at. It makes me wonder is the person on the bench a photographer or a hunter? Maybe they are waiting for someone? Who knows? Besides my few little suggestions I think that you did a very good job. Good Luck in future challenges. Please let me know if you think that I am way off base.<br/> <br/>mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I LOVE the colors! Very Nice!! I think that the lighting (contrast) is perfect too. Wouldn''t change it at ALL.  There are a few things I would change. Is that a light pole? There is a really tall pole or something behind or infront of the tree on the right. I would have cloned that out. I also would have cloned out the bridge in the background. It is a nice bridge...but doesn''t say wild safari to me.  The trees and the coloration of the sky combined with the sunset scream safari to me though. Reminds me of the beginning of The Lion King movie. Can you tell that I have small children? As far as the compostion goes, I think that you did a fine job. I held up a piece of paper and "cropped" off some on the left side where the negative space is. My thoughts were..."nope, looks better like it is!" With the negative space gone the picture looks too centered and boring.  The sun looks a little strange. I guess because I expect it to be a circle. Not sure how the two bumps on it happened....it was just something I noticed. Overall...I like the photograph! It is very pleasing to look at. It makes me wonder is the person on the bench a photographer or a hunter? Maybe they are waiting for someone? Who knows? Besides my few little suggestions I think that you did a very good job. Good Luck in future challenges. Please let me know if you think that I am way off base. mandy', '2005-12-14 20:56:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952457, 263847, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I really like the contrast between the color of the sand and the blue sky. It is really nice to be able to see the texture of the rock up close without the rest of the image really blurry. The sky looks fierce! It appears to be moving very quickly and the wave hitting against the shore also repeats the feeling of strength. Nature is amazing and you have captured it well. <br/> <br/>I would love to see this picture without the processing. There are some dark spots, but in a way it adds to the mood for me. I feel that the clouds are oversharpened. The edges are so sharp, that far away just seems unnatural. <br/> <br/>I would also like to add that I really like how you framed the image with the rocks starting in the upper left hand corner. My eyes flow right through the middle of the image, as the rocks seperate the land and sea in just the right spot. Please forgive my horrible spelling. I just read what I typed and I sound like a hippie....just a little.LOL Great image and good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I really like the contrast between the color of the sand and the blue sky. It is really nice to be able to see the texture of the rock up close without the rest of the image really blurry. The sky looks fierce! It appears to be moving very quickly and the wave hitting against the shore also repeats the feeling of strength. Nature is amazing and you have captured it well.  I would love to see this picture without the processing. There are some dark spots, but in a way it adds to the mood for me. I feel that the clouds are oversharpened. The edges are so sharp, that far away just seems unnatural.  I would also like to add that I really like how you framed the image with the rocks starting in the upper left hand corner. My eyes flow right through the middle of the image, as the rocks seperate the land and sea in just the right spot. Please forgive my horrible spelling. I just read what I typed and I sound like a hippie....just a little.LOL Great image and good luck in future challenges. Mandy', '2005-12-14 21:08:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952670, 262186, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I think this is amazing!!! The texture in the feathers looks so soft. Beautifully cropped. I would have given you a better comment during the challenge but there were so many to vote on. The colors are bright and look great. There does seem to be some noise. I was grasping for something to suggest and I had to look a long time to find that. It is just really hard for me to give suggestion to a photo as great as this one. So my critique is....AWESOME PHOTO! You kicked my butt. <br/>Sorry I am not very helpful.<br/> <br/>mandy<br/></td>', '*Critique Club* I think this is amazing!!! The texture in the feathers looks so soft. Beautifully cropped. I would have given you a better comment during the challenge but there were so many to vote on. The colors are bright and look great. There does seem to be some noise. I was grasping for something to suggest and I had to look a long time to find that. It is just really hard for me to give suggestion to a photo as great as this one. So my critique is....AWESOME PHOTO! You kicked my butt. Sorry I am not very helpful. mandy', '2005-12-14 22:24:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952742, 259418, 27763, '<td valign="top">This is awesome!  Loved it during the voting period and I love it now!</td>', 'This is awesome!  Loved it during the voting period and I love it now!', '2005-12-14 22:37:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1952894, 263629, 30625, '<td valign="top">Critique Club WoooHoooo<br/> <br/>Compostion: <br/>Compostion on portraits can be difficult when getting up close as you just dont know what elements of the portrait to keep and what to leave out. In this image I would have zoomed out or steped back a tad to create room for the chin. This would have significantly changed the aspect of the image and increased the level of the glasses to just above center and into the rule of thirds. I not 100% sure but it looks like your grandpa was smoking and maybe that would have shown good in this image. <br/> <br/>Technical &amp; Setup:<br/>Diffusing the light would have maybee eliminated the hard light on his Left eye glass lens. This would also removed the hot line under his hat and forehead.<br/> <br/>Camera Work: <br/>Not much to say in this column but keep up the good work on knowing your camera. It seems like you used a tripod. <br/> <br/>Post Processing:<br/>I checked the histogram on your image. You captured the flesh tones very well. <br/> <br/>My opinon:<br/>I would have graded this image between 60 and 65 out of 100. The image doesnt really do much as appeal for the free study challenge. This may also be due to the fact I know what kind of talent is out there to compete against in DPC. <br/> <br/>The beauty about a free study challenge is photographing the things that you love. <br/></td>', 'Critique Club WoooHoooo Compostion: Compostion on portraits can be difficult when getting up close as you just dont know what elements of the portrait to keep and what to leave out. In this image I would have zoomed out or steped back a tad to create room for the chin. This would have significantly changed the aspect of the image and increased the level of the glasses to just above center and into the rule of thirds. I not 100% sure but it looks like your grandpa was smoking and maybe that would have shown good in this image.  Technical & Setup:Diffusing the light would have maybee eliminated the hard light on his Left eye glass lens. This would also removed the hot line under his hat and forehead. Camera Work: Not much to say in this column but keep up the good work on knowing your camera. It seems like you used a tripod.  Post Processing:I checked the histogram on your image. You captured the flesh tones very well.  My opinon:I would have graded this image between 60 and 65 out of 100. The image doesnt really do much as appeal for the free study challenge. This may also be due to the fact I know what kind of talent is out there to compete against in DPC.  The beauty about a free study challenge is photographing the things that you love. ', '2005-12-14 23:26:39.000000', NULL, 0),
